{
 "source": "FCCA's Figures IX-1a to IX-1f (the Surround family), IX-2a to IX-2f (Blockage) and IX-3a to IX-3f (Buridan) [FCCA pp. 394-399 (img)], the eighteen layouts FCCA redraws from the book, read as 300 dpi crops of the page images (pdftoppm -r 300 -x -y -W -H) and compared object by object with the files of problems/ rendered by tools/render_problem.py (ANSWERS.md 4: the book's figure wins; docs/problems.md 6).",
 "method": "FCCA's figures are halftone scans: the icons are light grey and the H, E1, E2 labels and arrows, printed inside the frame, are black, so no ink threshold separates the icons from the arrows (at grey level 200 the touched object, its neighbours and the arrow form one cluster). The comparison is therefore by eye, object by object: for each figure, every object FCCA draws is listed with its type, its label and the ninth of the table it stands in, and checked against the file's object of that id (tests/test_ch2.py checks the type and the ninth). Two things were measured on the scans with tools/measure_figure.py: the frames (find_frame) and, by a column profile of the darkest pixel over the glasses' rows, the gaps of Blockage 6 and 9 (IX-2e, IX-2f).",
 "frame": "FCCA draws the table square: the eighteen frames measure 359-372 x 365-374 px inside their lines at 300 dpi (ratio 0.98-1.01), where the book's figures are 1.10 wider than tall (D-001). Positions are compared as fractions of the frame's inner width and height.",
